# ─── Supabase / Prisma Connection ──────────────────────────────────────────
# DATABASE_URL: Pooled runtime connection (pgBouncer via Supabase pooler).
#   Used by Prisma client at runtime — supports many concurrent short-lived
#   connections efficiently through connection pooling.
# DIRECT_URL: Direct (non-pooled) connection for Prisma migrations and seeding.
#   Bypasses pgBouncer — required because DDL operations need a direct session.
# ─── Supabase Auth (browser-safe) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL: The Supabase project API URL. Prefixed with
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_ so it is available in the browser for the Supabase JS client.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY: The Supabase publishable API key
#   (new key format, prefixed `sb_publishable_`). Browser-safe — this key
#   has limited permissions enforced by RLS policies.
# ─── Supabase Auth (server-only) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY: The Supabase secret API key (new key format, prefixed
#   `sb_secret_`). Server-only — this key bypasses RLS and must NEVER be
#   exposed to the browser or committed with a real value. Used for admin
#   operations (e.g. creating auth users from the seed script).
DATABASE_URL=
DIRECT_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# ─── Dev seed (pnpm db:seed) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Credentials are never defaulted in code; the seed fails if these are empty.
# SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL / SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD: the ADMIN account the seed creates.
# SEED_USER_PASSWORD: shared password for the 4 seeded normal users
#   (<name>@seed.comuninca.test).
# SEED_ALLOW_REMOTE: set to "true" to allow seeding a non-localhost
#   DIRECT_URL (e.g. the hosted Supabase project). The seed always refuses
#   NODE_ENV/VERCEL_ENV=production.
SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL=
SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
SEED_USER_PASSWORD=
SEED_ALLOW_REMOTE=
